## 9. Agent Prompt Guide

```
When implementing this design system:

1. **Color discipline:** Use ONLY the colors defined in Section 3.
   - Primary: {primary color} — reserved for main CTAs and active states
   - Never use primary for decorative elements or body text
   - Always check dark mode equivalents if implementing theme toggle

2. **Typography consistency:** Use ONLY the fonts and scale in Section 4.
   - Headings: {heading font} at exact sizes specified
   - Body: {body font} at exact sizes specified
   - Never mix more than 2 font families in any view

3. **Spacing rhythm:** Maintain consistent spacing using the system in Section 6.
   - Section padding: {value}
   - Component gaps: {value}
   - Never use arbitrary values — use the scale

4. **Component completeness:** Implement ALL states defined in Section 5.
   - Default, hover, active, disabled for all interactive elements
   - Error states for all form inputs
   - Loading states for async actions

5. **Elevation consistency:** Use shadow and radius scales from Section 7.
   - Cards: {level} shadow, {level} radius
   - Buttons: {level} radius
   - Modals: {level} shadow
   - Never invent new shadow values

6. **Responsive behavior:** Follow breakpoints in Section 6.
   - Mobile-first or desktop-first: {approach}
   - Key breakpoint changes: {description}
   - Test all components at all breakpoints

7. **Pattern adherence:** Follow {product type} patterns from Section 1.
   - {Type-specific rule 1}
   - {Type-specific rule 2}
   - {Type-specific rule 3}

8. **Check CSS Color Module L5 support** — Firefox needs `@supports not` fallback for BOTH dark AND light themes

9. **Implement z-index scale** — Don't use ad-hoc values; create systematic scale from Section 7 tokens

10. **Audit !important usage** — Should only be in `@layer overrides` if using CSS Layers (Section 10)

11. **Add :focus-visible styles** — Use `--focus-ring` token for all interactive elements (Section 11)

12. **Scope theme transitions** — Don't use universal `*` selector; target specific elements only

13. **Throttle scroll/resize handlers** — Use requestAnimationFrame pattern (Section 10)

14. **Transform not top/left** — Animate with transform/opacity for GPU acceleration, never width/height/margin

15. **Respect prefers-reduced-motion** — Test with OS reduced motion setting; disable non-essential animations

16. **Document browser support** — Note which modern features (Section 12) need fallbacks

17. **Fix accessibility gaps first** — Section 14 high-risk items (focus, contrast, motion) before visual polish

18. **Follow token compliance** — No hardcoded values; use Section 3 tokens exclusively

19. **Check CSS Layers order** — If @layer present, ensure all styles are layered (no unlayered overrides)

20. **Verify landmark elements** — Use semantic HTML: header, nav, main, footer, article, section

21. **Implement heading hierarchy** — Single H1 per page, no skipped levels (Section 11)

22. **Add ARIA labels** — All interactive elements need accessible names (Section 11)

23. **Optimize animation budget** — Limit simultaneous animations (Section 13); composite only properties

24. **Validate WCAG contrast** — All text meets 4.5:1 minimum; large text 3:1 minimum
```

